refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Dom\HTMLCollectionDom\Element::getElementsByClassName stringclassNames
Returns a Dom\HTMLCollection of the descendants of this element, in document order, whose class attribute contains all the classes given in classNames. The element itself is never part of the collection.

&reftitle.errors;

 Throws a ValueError if
 classNames contains a null byte.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Dom\Element::getElementsByClassName example


<?php

$dom = Dom\HTMLDocument::createFromString(
    '<!DOCTYPE html><body><div id="list">'
        . '<p class="item new">One</p>'
        . '<p class="item">Two</p>'
        . '<p class="Item">Three</p>'
        . '</div></body>',
    LIBXML_NOERROR
);

$list = $dom->getElementById('list');

foreach ($list->getElementsByClassName('new  item') as $element) {
    echo $element->textContent, "\n";
}

echo $list->getElementsByClassName('item')->length, "\n";


   &example.outputs;


One
2
